{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_43","type":"agent_message","text":"The WebGPU problem came from the browser launch flags: adding an explicit SwiftShader ANGLE backend makes the minimal GPU check draw correctly. The virtual-display review also confirms the scene renders. I’ve added camera tilt and a farewell wave; the next test will check the whole journey, including creek crossings, tuning, flight, saves, and shared-world synchronization."}}
