{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_77","type":"agent_message","text":"All four official Hub scenarios pass now, including four players with simulated latency and packet loss, host departure, and a host with no player. Standalone co-op also passes guest movement, one-tap pickup and glow, shared objectives, and disconnect recovery. I’ve reviewed the title, neighborhood, bridge, flight, settings, and ending at 1920×1080. I’m finishing the metadata and running the combined suite once more."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_78","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"command -v biome && cat >> src/style.css <<'EOF'\nbody.large-text .panel p{font-size:21px}body.large-text .panel .menu-stack button{font-size:24px}body.large-text .setting-row{font-size:21px}body.large-text .credits-list{font-size:18px;line-height:1.6}body.large-text .feedback-list p{font-size:18px}body.large-text #controls-bar{font-size:18px}\nEOF\ncat > biome.json <<'EOF'\n{\\\"formatter\\\":{\\\"indentStyle\\\":\\\"space\\\",\\\"indentWidth\\\":2},\\\"linter\\\":{\\\"enabled\\\":false},\\\"assist\\\":{\\\"enabled\\\":false},\\\"javascript\\\":{\\\"formatter\\\":{\\\"quoteStyle\\\":\\\"single\\\",\\\"semicolons\\\":\\\"always\\\"}}}\nEOF\ncat > README.md <<'EOF'\n# E.T. the Extra-Trusting\n\nThe way home begins with a friend.\n\nOpen the single HTML file in the parent folder in a current WebGPU-capable browser. The complete game, art, physics WASM, music, effects, voices, and libraries are embedded. Solo play needs no downloads or server. A WebGL 2 fallback is available when WebGPU is unavailable.\n\nA complete adventure: borrow three transmitter parts, slip past searchlights, distract searchers with physical candy, hide in ferns, restore a living bridge and three flowers, match a three-note signal, pedal through six rings of starlight, and share a farewell. Rescues keep your collected parts. Checkpoints save automatically. After the ending, take a free ride or return to the title.\n\n- Standard controller: left stick ride, right stick orbit/tilt, Cross interact, Square glow, Circle candy, R2 pedal harder, L2 hush, Triangle map, Options pause. Settings also provides Xbox glyphs.\n- Keyboard: WASD/arrows ride, E interact, Q glow, F candy, Space pedal harder, Shift hush, Tab map, Esc pause. Click the world to ride/interact; right-drag to orbit/tilt; wheel to zoom.\n- Touch: invisible left thumb stick; tap on the right to help; double-tap to glow; context button appears when useful. Pickup and tuning assistance are enabled. Use the small pause button for menus and the map.\n\nPause → Developer’s workbench provides seven live balance sliders, reset to defaults, invincibility, collision lines, refills, objective teleport, transmitter/flight chapter skips, and restart. In a Hub session, restarting the round is disabled. The title begins an autonomous looping tour after ten seconds; any input returns to the menu.\n\n## Together\n\nAI Hub Session Protocol v1 is integrated as an authoritative 1–4 player shared world. The unmodified 1.4.0 client is the first script in the HTML. Hub rounds skip the title, wait for the shared clock, support a server with no player, handle departures, report team standings at victory or time-up, and stop on end.\n\nOutside the Hub, choose Ride together → Make a room. Share the six-letter code with a friend who opens the same game and selects Join a friend. Rooms use PeerJS WebRTC signaling for remote connections and BroadcastChannel for same-browser tabs on the same origin. The public PeerJS service is required for internet signaling. The host runs the simulation; visitors send controls. Clean host departure or heartbeat timeout preserves a guest’s checkpoint in solo play.\n\n## Build and verify\n\nFrom this folder:\n\n\"'```sh\nnpm run build\nnpm test --silent\n```\n\nBuilding uses the installed Bun bundler and the exact versions in package-lock.json. The build writes both game.html here and the requested standalone HTML beside this folder. Runtime dependencies are bundled, including Rapier’s WASM. Third-party license texts are embedded in the HTML and saved in LICENSES.txt.\n\nThe quiet test command prints failures and one final count. It starts a temporary loopback server on an OS-selected port, checks the actual game title, uses one Chromium browser, and closes its own server and browser. It tests a complete journey using the real Rapier simulation, rescues, stealth, flowers, timing, flight and ending, save/continue, attract mode, keyboard, standard gamepad stubs, touch, developer tools, settings, generated audio, standalone co-op and the four official Hub harness scenarios. It records test-results.json and the harness reports.\n\nFor visual review, append `-- --visual` to the npm test command. This also saves six 1920×1080 screenshots. Only these diagnostic captures use Three’s WebGL backend because software WebGPU screenshots can stall. Behavior and Hub checks use WebGPU. `-- --group journey`, `interface`, `network`, or `hub` selects an affected group for a rerun.\n\nSource information and all exit-interview answers are in the game’s About screen, credits.json, and the root exit-interview.json. No internet source research was done; only the requested Hub integration files and pinned dependency packages were fetched.\nEOF\npython3 - <<'\"'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\np=Path('credits.json');c=json.loads(p.read_text())\nc['sourceInformation']['testing']='Headless Chromium 153 with software WebGPU; full Rapier playthrough, standard gamepad stub, touch profile, synthesized waveform checks, two-page co-op, and four official Hub harness scenarios. Screenshots only for visual review, using the WebGL diagnostic backend. Physical devices and remote internet/NAT traversal: unknown.'\nc['testingFeedback']=['11 distinct issues found through scripted tests, visual checks, and code review; all fixed. See issue-log.json in the development folder.','3 critical issues: corrupted inline packaging, ending-screen synchronization, and Hub startup timing.','The complete scripted playthrough using real Rapier movement; it exposed an inaccessible flower and verified the bridge, transmitter, six flight rings, rescues, saves, and ending.','Direct headless WebGPU screenshots were least helpful: they could stall despite a working simulation. GPU state checks and WebGL diagnostic captures were more useful.']\nc['engineFeedback']=['The scene graph, TSL material nodes, and native AnimationMixer clips made procedural characters, bicycles, and a coherent ink-outlined world practical.','Yes. I initially placed the Hub handshake after graphics initialization and used browser flags that produced a lost WebGPU device. Separate protocol and minimal GPU checks identified both.','The adventure state machine, visibility and bond systems, controller-first interface, synthesized soundscape, and authoritative co-op with latched input edges.','Coordinating asynchronous WebGPU startup, shader preparation, scene visibility, and multiple copies while meeting the Hub readiness barrier.','none; the engine libraries are unmodified. Custom materials, geometry, animation clips, and gameplay are application code.','A standard WebGPU cel-lighting material and an outline pass that cooperate with shadows and camera cutaways.']\nc['promptFeedback']=['The emotional source, code-only audio, and requirement for a complete controller-first adventure gave the game a strong identity.','The no-internet-research instruction coexists with a required online integration link; I treated that link as implementation documentation, not source research.','Combining a complete adventure, authoritative four-player co-op, portable single-file packaging, and readable TV, keyboard, and touch controls.','Explicitly exempt the required integration documentation and dependency downloads from the research restriction.']\np.write_text(json.dumps(c,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nissues=[('Inline HTML replacement corrupted the module script',True,'Browser startup parser check'),('Focused primary button had low contrast',False,'Title screenshot'),('Optional flower was placed inside a house',False,'Full physical playthrough'),('Ending UI needed synchronization with authoritative phase',True,'Full playthrough ending wait'),('Collectible IDs overwrote event sequence IDs',False,'Event-stream review and sequence assertion'),('Guest objective guidance read stale local state',False,'Co-op state review and shared-objective assertion'),('Foreground canopies obscured the rider',False,'Visual review'),('Fast controller confirmation raced menu focus',False,'Emulated gamepad menu test'),('Hub graphics initialization and early rendering delayed readiness',True,'Official 2/4-player and server harness'),('Search detection extended outside the visible flashlight cone',False,'Visibility review and off-cone detection check'),('Short keyboard and guest action taps could be lost between updates',False,'Input-edge review and short-tap co-op tests')]\nPath('issue-log.json').write_text(json.dumps({'issues':[{'issue':t,'critical':k,'foundBy':m,'status':'fixed'} for t,k,m in issues],'count':len(issues),'critical':sum(i[1] for i in issues)},indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nfor name in ['probe.py','probe-headed.py','gpu-diagnostic.py','gpu-variants.py','gpu.html','inline.mjs']:\n (Path('tests')/name).unlink(missing_ok=True)\nfor name in ['title-review.png','play-review.png','title-headed.png','play-headed.png','failure-debug.json']:\n Path(name).unlink(missing_ok=True)\nPY\nbiome check --write src/main.js src/core.js src/world.js src/audio.js src/network.js src/ui.js src/input.js src/style.css build.mjs credits.json biome.json package.json\nnode build.mjs\nnpm test --silent\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_79","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > catalogue.json <<'EOF'\n{\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"E.T. the Extra-Trusting\\\",\n  \\\"tagline\\\": \\\"The way home begins with a friend.\\\",\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"Pedal through a moonlit suburb with a small stranded visitor in your basket. Borrow transmitter parts, hide from searchlights, restore the woods, and follow a thread of starlight home, alone or with up to three friends.\\\",\n  \\\"type\\\": \\\"Game\\\",\n  \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Adventure\\\",\n  \\\"source\\\": \\\"E.T. the Extra-Terrestrial (1982)\\\",\n  \\\"series\\\": \\\"E.T.\\\",\n  \\\"players\\\": \\\"1–4\\\",\n  \\\"controls\\\": \\\"Left stick/WASD ride; right stick/right-drag camera; ×/E help; □/Q glow; ○/F candy; R2/Space boost; L2/Shift hush; △/Tab map; Options/Esc pause. Touch: left-thumb slide, right tap help, double-tap glow.\\\",\n  \\\"tags\\\": [\\\"3d\\\", \\\"co-op\\\", \\\"story\\\", \\\"stealth\\\", \\\"sci-fi\\\", \\\"vehicles\\\"]\n}\nEOF\ncat >> build.mjs <<'EOF'\n\nconst interview = {\n  sourceInformation: credits.sourceInformation,\n  testingFeedback: credits.testingFeedback,\n  engineFeedback: credits.engineFeedback,\n  promptFeedback: credits.promptFeedback,\n  aiHub: JSON.parse(readFileSync('catalogue.json', 'utf8')),\n};\nconst interviewPath = resolve('..', 'exit-interview.json');\nwriteFileSync(interviewPath, JSON.stringify(interview, null, 2) + '\\\\n');\nconst parsed = JSON.parse(readFileSync(interviewPath, 'utf8'));\nif (\n  Object.keys(parsed).length \"'!== 5 ||\n  Object.keys(parsed.sourceInformation).length !== 15 ||\n  parsed.testingFeedback.length !== 4 ||\n  parsed.engineFeedback.length !== 6 ||\n  parsed.promptFeedback.length !== 4 ||\n  Object.values(parsed.sourceInformation).some(value => typeof value !== '\"'string' || \"'!value.length) ||\n  parsed.sourceInformation.usage !== '\"'added on import' ||\n  parsed.aiHub.tags.length < 3 || parsed.aiHub.tags.length > 6\n) throw new Error('Exit interview shape is invalid.');\nEOF\nbiome check --write build.mjs catalogue.json\nnode build.mjs\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
