g, save/continue, attract mode, keyboard, standard gamepad stubs, touch, developer tools, settings, generated audio, standalone co-op and the four official Hub harness scenarios. It records test-results.json and the harness reports.\n\nFor visual review, append `-- --visual` to the npm test command. This also saves six 1920×1080 screenshots. Only these diagnostic captures use Three’s WebGL backend because software WebGPU screenshots can stall. Behavior and Hub checks use WebGPU. `-- --group journey`, `interface`, `network`, or `hub` selects an affected group for a rerun.\n\nSource information and all exit-interview answers are in the game’s About screen, credits.json, and the root exit-interview.json. No internet source research was done; only the requested Hub integration files and pinned dependency packages were fetched.\nEOF\npython3 - <<'\"'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\np=Path('credits.json');c=json.loads(p.read_text())\nc['sourceInformation']['testing']='Headless Chromium 153 with software WebGPU; full Rapier playthrough, standard gamepad stub, touch profile, synthesized waveform checks, two-page co-op, and four official Hub harness scenarios. Screenshots only for visual review, using the WebGL diagnostic backend. Physical devices and remote internet/NAT traversal: unknown.'\nc['testingFeedback']=['11 distinct issues found through scripted tests, visual checks, and code review; all fixed. See issue-log.json in the development folder.','3 critical issues: corrupted inline packaging, ending-screen synchronization, and Hub startup timing.','The complete scripted playthrough using real Rapier movement; it exposed an inaccessible flower and verified the bridge, transmitter, six flight rings, rescues, saves, and ending.','Direct headless WebGPU screenshots were least helpful: they could stall despite a working simulation. GPU state checks and WebGL diagnostic captures were more useful.']\nc['engineFeedback']=['The scene graph, TSL material nodes, and native AnimationMixer clips made procedural characters, bicycles, and a coherent ink-outlined world practical.','Yes. I initially placed the Hub handshake after graphics initialization and used browser flags that produced a lost WebGPU device. Separate protocol and minimal GPU checks identified both.','The adventure state machine, visibility and bond systems, controller-first interface, synthesized soundscape, and authoritative co-op with latched input edges.','Coordinating asynchronous WebGPU startup, shader preparation, scene visibility, and multiple copies while meeting the Hub readiness barrier.','none; the engine libraries are unmodified. Custom materials, geometry, animation clips, and gameplay are application code.','A standard WebGPU cel-lighting material and an outline pass that cooperate with shadows and camera cutaways.']\nc['promptFeedback']=['The emotional source, code-only audio, and requirement for a complete controller-first adventure gave the game a strong identity.','The no-internet-research instruction coexists with a required online integration link; I treated that link as implementation documentation, not source research.','Combining a complete adventure, authoritative four-player co-op, portable single-file packaging, and readable TV, keyboard, and touch controls.','Explicitly exempt the required integration documentation and dependency downloads from the research restriction.']\np.write_text(json.dumps(c,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nissues=[('Inline HTML replacement corrupted the module script',True,'Browser startup parser check'),('Focused primary button had low contrast',False,'Title screenshot'),('Optional flower was placed inside a house',False,'Full physical playthrough'),('Ending UI needed synchronization with authoritative phase',True,'Full playthrough ending wait'),('Collectible IDs overwrote event sequence IDs',False,'Event-stream review and sequence assertion'),('Guest objective guidance read stale local state',False,'Co-op state review and shared-objective assertion'),('Foreground canopies obscured the rider',False,'Visual review'),('Fast controller confirmation raced menu focus',False,'Emulated gamepad menu test'),('Hub graphics initialization and early rendering delayed readiness',True,'Official 2/4-player and server harness'),('Search detection extended outside the visible flashlight cone',False,'Visibility review and off-cone detection check'),('Short keyboard and guest action taps could be lost between updates',False,'Input-edge review and short-tap co-op tests')]\nPath('issue-log.json').write_text(json.dumps({'issues':[{'issue':t,'critical':k,'foundBy':m,'status':'fixed'} for t,k,m in issues],'count':len(issues),'critical':sum(i[1] for i in issues)},indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nfor name in ['probe.py','probe-headed.py','gpu-diagnostic.py','gpu-variants.py','gpu.html','inline.mjs']:\n (Path('tests')/name).unlink(missing_ok=True)\nfor name in ['title-review.png','play-review.png','title-headed.png','play-headed.png','failure-debug.json']:\n Path(name).unlink(missing_ok=True)\nPY\nbiome check --write src/main.js src/core.js src/world.js src/audio.js src/network.js src/ui.js src/input.js src/style.css build.mjs credits.json biome.json package.json\nnode build.mjs\nnpm test --silent\"","aggregated_output":"/home/micha/.local/bin/biome\nChecked 12 files in 20ms. Fixed 11 files.\nBuilt E.T.-the-Extra-Trusting-ET-the-Extra-Terrestrial-1982-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261105-191342.html\n129 checks · 0 failures\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_81","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json,hashlib\nstem=json.loads(Path('selection.json').read_text())['stem']\nroot=Path('..')\na=(root/(stem+'.html')).read_bytes();b=Path('game.html').read_bytes();html=a.decode()\nclient=Path('vendor/session.js').read_text()\nfirst=html.split('<script>',1)[1].split('</script>',1)[0]\ninfo=json.loads((root/'exit-interview.json').read_text())\nassert a==b\nassert first==client\nassert set(info)=={'sourceInformation','testingFeedback','engineFeedback','promptFeedback','aiHub'}\nassert info['aiHub']['name']==json.loads(Path('selection.json').read_text())['title']\nassert info['sourceInformation']['usage']=='added on import'\nassert len(info['testingFeedback'])==4 and len(info['engineFeedback'])==6 and len(info['promptFeedback'])==4\nassert '/*CREDITS_DATA*/' not in html and '<\"'!--GAME_SCRIPT-->'\"' not in html and '/*INLINE_CSS*/' not in html\nassert 'third-party-licenses' in html\nprint(json.dumps({'htmlBytes':len(a),'sha256':hashlib.sha256(a).hexdigest(),'exitInterview':'valid JSON; exact root keys; complete answers','hubClient':'unmodified first script','rootFiles':[p.name for p in root.iterdir() if p.is_file()]},indent=2))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
